1
00:01:32,860 --> 00:01:35,020
[Forging Justice]

2
00:01:35,280 --> 00:01:37,660
[Episode 21]

3
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:40,259
Thirty tables?

4
00:01:41,400 --> 00:01:42,430
Are you trying to get me

5
00:01:42,430 --> 00:01:43,400
to retire early?

6
00:01:48,070 --> 00:01:49,600
Dad, I'll pay for it myself.

7
00:01:49,759 --> 00:01:51,560
You don't have to pay. It's fine.

8
00:01:52,479 --> 00:01:53,080
Nonsense.

9
00:01:58,350 --> 00:01:59,750
I am the court president.

10
00:01:59,870 --> 00:02:00,480
Can you guarantee

11
00:02:00,480 --> 00:02:01,920
that among all the guests,

12
00:02:01,920 --> 00:02:03,450
no one wants a favor from me?

13
00:02:03,560 --> 00:02:05,590
Can you guarantee every gift money

14
00:02:05,680 --> 00:02:06,540
is above board?

15
00:02:07,430 --> 00:02:09,190
Can you guarantee that people won't

16
00:02:09,190 --> 00:02:11,190
gossip about this behind our backs?

17
00:02:14,150 --> 00:02:16,070
Dad, a court president is also human.

18
00:02:16,070 --> 00:02:17,470
You have to live your life.

19
00:02:17,470 --> 00:02:20,100
We can't shut ourselves off
from all human connections.

20
00:02:20,100 --> 00:02:21,360
But we can't apply it here,

21
00:02:21,360 --> 00:02:21,890
you know?

22
00:02:23,680 --> 00:02:25,210
Except for your classmates

23
00:02:25,590 --> 00:02:26,800
and my colleagues,

24
00:02:27,280 --> 00:02:27,880
no one else

25
00:02:28,150 --> 00:02:29,079
is to be invited.

26
00:02:29,470 --> 00:02:31,400
No red envelopes. Keep it low-key.

27
00:02:31,590 --> 00:02:32,120
And also,

28
00:02:32,430 --> 00:02:33,910
that buddy of yours, Li Xiang,

29
00:02:33,910 --> 00:02:35,170
the one at the law firm,

30
00:02:36,150 --> 00:02:37,030
he cannot come.

31
00:02:37,590 --> 00:02:38,840
It would just look too suspicious.

32
00:02:38,840 --> 00:02:39,280
Dad.

33
00:02:39,560 --> 00:02:40,800
Are we handling a case?

34
00:02:40,800 --> 00:02:42,530
Why are we practicing recusal?

35
00:02:42,710 --> 00:02:43,560
I knew it.

36
00:02:44,310 --> 00:02:46,030
You must be the one behind this,

37
00:02:46,030 --> 00:02:47,630
telling him to make a fuss, right?

38
00:02:47,630 --> 00:02:48,250
No, no.

39
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:49,590
Yes, it was me.

40
00:02:50,310 --> 00:02:51,510
I told him to. So what?

41
00:02:52,280 --> 00:02:53,630
Dad, you are the court president.

42
00:02:53,630 --> 00:02:54,400
So for all these years,

43
00:02:54,400 --> 00:02:55,400
you've kept saying no to this and that.

44
00:02:55,400 --> 00:02:56,150
I endured it all.

45
00:02:56,150 --> 00:02:57,630
I didn't say anything, did I?

46
00:02:57,630 --> 00:02:58,910
But this is my wedding.

47
00:02:59,360 --> 00:03:01,290
I'm only doing this once in my life.

48
00:03:02,080 --> 00:03:02,960
Mom is gone,

49
00:03:03,310 --> 00:03:05,510
and you're just brushing me off, right?

50
00:03:05,750 --> 00:03:07,430
If we can't accept red envelopes

51
00:03:07,430 --> 00:03:08,360
and can't invite people,

52
00:03:08,360 --> 00:03:09,470
then what's the point of having a wedding?

53
00:03:09,470 --> 00:03:12,070
Might as well just have
a New Year's Eve dinner.

54
00:03:13,870 --> 00:03:15,430
We'll keep it simple.

55
00:03:16,030 --> 00:03:16,960
Just two tables.

56
00:03:18,590 --> 00:03:19,390
That's final.

57
00:03:21,240 --> 00:03:22,240
Listen to your dad.

58
00:03:22,240 --> 00:03:22,970
Be sensible.

59
00:03:27,640 --> 00:03:28,630
Am I not sensible?

60
00:03:28,630 --> 00:03:29,140
No, no.

61
00:03:29,360 --> 00:03:30,420
It's not about you.

62
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:33,660
Alright, alright, calm down.

63
00:03:41,310 --> 00:03:42,770
Why can't he be sentenced?

64
00:03:43,310 --> 00:03:44,430
Doesn't he have to obey the law?

65
00:03:44,430 --> 00:03:45,590
Do whatever he wants?

66
00:03:45,590 --> 00:03:46,470
No, look.

67
00:03:46,630 --> 00:03:48,710
He's a person with limited civil capacity.

68
00:03:48,710 --> 00:03:49,280
He can't

69
00:03:49,280 --> 00:03:50,800
be held accountable for his actions.

70
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:51,800
What kind of person?

71
00:03:51,800 --> 00:03:52,600
I'll kill you!

72
00:03:52,910 --> 00:03:53,710
I'll kill you!

73
00:03:56,630 --> 00:03:57,470
A person with limited civil capacity...

74
00:03:57,470 --> 00:03:58,750
Don't give me that nonsense.

75
00:03:58,750 --> 00:03:59,880
I don't understand.

76
00:04:00,960 --> 00:04:02,240
I can explain it to you.

77
00:04:02,590 --> 00:04:03,080
It means

78
00:04:03,080 --> 00:04:04,310
that when Yin Ping set fire

79
00:04:04,310 --> 00:04:05,640
to your livestock shed,

80
00:04:05,800 --> 00:04:06,660
he wasn't aware

81
00:04:07,150 --> 00:04:08,470
of what he was doing.

82
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:09,590
Get it?

83
00:04:12,560 --> 00:04:13,430
I don't get it!

84
00:04:13,800 --> 00:04:15,750
I came to you because I respect the law.

85
00:04:15,750 --> 00:04:17,950
You can't just sweep this under the rug!

86
00:04:19,430 --> 00:04:21,029
If he doesn't know anything,

87
00:04:21,269 --> 00:04:22,480
then how come when he saw her,

88
00:04:22,480 --> 00:04:24,340
he yelled, "So white! So white!"?

89
00:04:26,160 --> 00:04:26,950
Don't bring up things

90
00:04:26,950 --> 00:04:28,280
unrelated to this case.

91
00:04:30,480 --> 00:04:32,040
Then who will compensate for our loss?

92
00:04:32,040 --> 00:04:32,570
Will you?

93
00:04:33,190 --> 00:04:35,120
I think you should calm down first.

94
00:04:35,600 --> 00:04:37,390
Fortunately, the livestock weren't hurt,

95
00:04:37,390 --> 00:04:37,800
right?

96
00:04:37,870 --> 00:04:39,270
Only the shed collapsed.

97
00:04:39,800 --> 00:04:41,390
Let's go talk to the village committee.

98
00:04:41,390 --> 00:04:42,240
Let's see if we can

99
00:04:42,240 --> 00:04:43,270
come up with a solution.

100
00:04:43,270 --> 00:04:44,680
What solution?

101
00:04:45,770 --> 00:04:46,650
He's a menace!

102
00:04:46,680 --> 00:04:49,540
He's going to cause a huge disaster
sooner or later!

103
00:04:50,950 --> 00:04:52,750
So you can't do anything, right?

104
00:04:53,390 --> 00:04:53,800
Fine.

105
00:04:55,680 --> 00:04:57,740
Next time I'll take care of it myself.

106
00:05:00,480 --> 00:05:00,920
Gun!

107
00:05:01,270 --> 00:05:02,920
Gun! My gun!

108
00:05:03,240 --> 00:05:04,040
Deal with him?

109
00:05:04,830 --> 00:05:05,560
How?

110
00:05:05,630 --> 00:05:07,430
Tell me, what am I supposed to do?

111
00:05:07,920 --> 00:05:09,250
His parents died early.

112
00:05:09,510 --> 00:05:11,000
It's just him and his grandma at home.

113
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:12,510
She can barely take care of herself,

114
00:05:12,510 --> 00:05:13,910
let alone look after him.

115
00:05:14,240 --> 00:05:14,950
Then can we send him

116
00:05:14,950 --> 00:05:16,480
to a psychiatric hospital?

117
00:05:17,390 --> 00:05:18,450
Who will pay for it?

118
00:05:19,270 --> 00:05:21,270
The government should provide relief.

119
00:05:21,270 --> 00:05:22,330
It won't cost much.

120
00:05:22,390 --> 00:05:23,510
Well, no matter how much it costs,

121
00:05:23,510 --> 00:05:24,910
someone has to pay for it.

122
00:05:26,390 --> 00:05:27,750
My way's the cheapest.

123
00:05:32,800 --> 00:05:33,870
I paid for it myself.

124
00:05:33,870 --> 00:05:34,310
No.

125
00:05:46,270 --> 00:05:47,070
Village Chief.

126
00:05:47,070 --> 00:05:47,510
Ma'am.

127
00:05:47,870 --> 00:05:49,470
Ping got into trouble again?

128
00:05:50,480 --> 00:05:51,740
Just lie down and rest.

129
00:05:53,360 --> 00:05:54,390
Sorry to bother you again.

130
00:05:54,390 --> 00:05:55,390
No trouble at all.

131
00:06:02,560 --> 00:06:03,720
Don't move!

132
00:06:09,920 --> 00:06:10,360
Lihui.

133
00:06:11,310 --> 00:06:11,640
Here.

134
00:06:12,750 --> 00:06:14,210
Send these out separately

135
00:06:14,430 --> 00:06:15,560
to the original trial court

136
00:06:15,560 --> 00:06:17,420
and the original procuratorate.

137
00:06:18,310 --> 00:06:20,000
Aren't we going to report
to the procuratorate first?

138
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:20,480
No need.

139
00:06:21,380 --> 00:06:22,920
We'll send them in the names of

140
00:06:22,920 --> 00:06:24,980
Prosecutor Guo Dajie and Zhang Lihui

141
00:06:25,070 --> 00:06:26,470
from the Bieshan Prison.

142
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:28,430
Um...

143
00:06:28,800 --> 00:06:30,000
Is this appropriate, Mentor?

144
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:30,920
It's fine.

145
00:06:31,630 --> 00:06:33,070
What if

146
00:06:33,120 --> 00:06:34,680
the procuratorate disagrees?

147
00:06:34,680 --> 00:06:36,159
Then should we send these materials

148
00:06:36,159 --> 00:06:36,920
or not?

149
00:06:40,190 --> 00:06:40,650
Mentor.

150
00:06:42,040 --> 00:06:43,480
I don't think your surname should be Guo.

151
00:06:43,480 --> 00:06:44,540
It should be Jiang.

152
00:06:44,800 --> 00:06:45,800
What? What Jiang?

153
00:06:46,510 --> 00:06:47,950
''Jiang'' is always the spiciest!

154
00:06:47,950 --> 00:06:48,310
Hey.

155
00:06:49,070 --> 00:06:49,470
You...

156
00:06:49,920 --> 00:06:50,270
Hey.

157
00:06:50,680 --> 00:06:51,070
You...

158
00:06:51,070 --> 00:06:53,270
Don't you think what I said makes sense?

159
00:06:54,310 --> 00:06:55,310
You kid...

160
00:07:08,680 --> 00:07:09,120
Guo.

161
00:07:10,040 --> 00:07:12,300
It's enough that we received the appeal.

162
00:07:12,560 --> 00:07:13,420
Anything extra

163
00:07:13,600 --> 00:07:16,000
should be handled
by the original trial court.

164
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:17,400
If we interfere too much,

165
00:07:17,600 --> 00:07:19,160
it will cause trouble

166
00:07:19,190 --> 00:07:20,720
for the local authorities.

167
00:07:21,190 --> 00:07:22,070
Yes, yes.

168
00:07:22,950 --> 00:07:23,800
Well,

169
00:07:24,270 --> 00:07:25,000
we have

170
00:07:25,720 --> 00:07:27,240
studied this case file

171
00:07:27,270 --> 00:07:29,360
carefully and repeatedly.

172
00:07:30,830 --> 00:07:31,750
We believe

173
00:07:32,110 --> 00:07:33,440
there is a real problem.

174
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:35,680
Discovering problems

175
00:07:35,680 --> 00:07:36,630
and representing inmates

176
00:07:36,630 --> 00:07:37,870
to seek legal relief

177
00:07:38,540 --> 00:07:39,970
is also part of

178
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:41,480
our job responsibilities.

179
00:07:41,480 --> 00:07:41,950
Right?

180
00:07:43,560 --> 00:07:45,510
All right, just leave it here for now.

181
00:07:45,510 --> 00:07:46,440
I have a meeting.

182
00:07:49,600 --> 00:07:50,460
Comrade Lihui,

183
00:07:50,560 --> 00:07:51,720
aren't you coming back yet?

184
00:07:51,720 --> 00:07:53,270
We have several positions waiting for you

185
00:07:53,270 --> 00:07:54,530
at the procuratorate.

186
00:07:55,750 --> 00:07:56,310
Prosecutor You,

187
00:07:56,310 --> 00:07:57,560
I'm tied up

188
00:07:57,560 --> 00:07:58,430
with this case.

189
00:07:58,630 --> 00:08:00,560
I'm waiting for you to cut me loose.

190
00:08:01,190 --> 00:08:02,870
You taught her all this, didn't you?

191
00:08:02,870 --> 00:08:03,680
Every line,

192
00:08:04,120 --> 00:08:05,120
sharp as a tack.

193
00:08:13,040 --> 00:08:13,570
Let's go.

194
00:08:14,510 --> 00:08:15,040
Let's go.

195
00:08:21,310 --> 00:08:21,950
Mentor,

196
00:08:22,630 --> 00:08:24,830
did you see Prosecutor You's attitude?

197
00:08:25,600 --> 00:08:27,600
Looks like we can only push this far.

198
00:08:28,390 --> 00:08:30,320
[Linshan City People's Procuratorate]

199
00:08:28,510 --> 00:08:30,070
How about we go to Nanlu?

200
00:08:33,480 --> 00:08:34,600
Talk to them face to face

201
00:08:34,600 --> 00:08:36,600
and force them to take it seriously.

202
00:08:38,960 --> 00:08:39,480
Mentor,

203
00:08:40,030 --> 00:08:41,480
if you have any concerns,

204
00:08:41,870 --> 00:08:42,870
I'll go by myself.

205
00:08:43,150 --> 00:08:44,030
What concerns would I have?

206
00:08:44,030 --> 00:08:45,160
I'm about to retire.

207
00:08:46,630 --> 00:08:47,830
What can they do to me?

208
00:08:48,870 --> 00:08:50,720
I'm concerned about you.

209
00:08:51,270 --> 00:08:53,000
You're disregarding leadership,

210
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:54,120
acting without authorization,

211
00:08:54,120 --> 00:08:55,200
lacking perspective,

212
00:08:55,200 --> 00:08:56,530
and asking for trouble.

213
00:08:58,670 --> 00:08:59,730
Go buy the tickets.

214
00:09:01,910 --> 00:09:02,750
How many?

215
00:09:03,320 --> 00:09:04,360
How many should I buy?

216
00:09:04,360 --> 00:09:05,360
What do you think?

217
00:09:05,390 --> 00:09:06,120
Two tickets.

218
00:09:31,270 --> 00:09:33,910
Two places, one heart.

219
00:09:35,270 --> 00:09:37,960
After a 13-year journey of love,

220
00:09:38,030 --> 00:09:39,600
our lawyer Lu Zeming

221
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:41,530
and Vice Principal Ding Rui

222
00:09:42,030 --> 00:09:43,560
have finally tied the knot,

223
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:46,130
building a happy and blissful family.

224
00:09:46,910 --> 00:09:48,960
This is the power of food!

225
00:09:49,600 --> 00:09:51,270
This is the miracle of love!

226
00:09:52,720 --> 00:09:54,600
What is the power of food?

227
00:09:54,630 --> 00:09:56,360
Tell us more about it.

228
00:09:57,840 --> 00:09:59,270
What is the power of food?

229
00:09:59,360 --> 00:10:00,760
This is a romantic story.

230
00:10:00,870 --> 00:10:01,750
We'll let the groom

231
00:10:01,750 --> 00:10:03,280
tell you all about it later.

232
00:10:03,670 --> 00:10:04,320
Let us

233
00:10:05,120 --> 00:10:06,240
wish the newlyweds

234
00:10:06,360 --> 00:10:07,760
a lifetime of happiness.

235
00:10:07,910 --> 00:10:09,120
May they grow old together.

236
00:10:09,120 --> 00:10:10,450
And to my former leader,

237
00:10:10,670 --> 00:10:12,000
Court Pres. Ding Zhongxiang,

238
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:12,910
good health

239
00:10:13,600 --> 00:10:14,960
and grandchildren soon!

240
00:10:14,960 --> 00:10:15,360
Great!

241
00:10:16,600 --> 00:10:17,030
Great!

242
00:10:17,930 --> 00:10:18,720
Now let's have

243
00:10:18,720 --> 00:10:20,120
the groom say a few words.

244
00:10:20,420 --> 00:10:21,270
You go ahead, or should I?

245
00:10:21,270 --> 00:10:22,330
Just say whatever.

246
00:10:25,480 --> 00:10:26,410
Eat up, drink up!

247
00:10:26,630 --> 00:10:27,390
Good!

248
00:10:28,080 --> 00:10:29,340
We're all family here.

249
00:10:31,120 --> 00:10:31,960
Great, great!

250
00:10:33,200 --> 00:10:34,200
Let's hurry down.

251
00:10:34,840 --> 00:10:35,360
Dad.

252
00:10:35,380 --> 00:10:36,000
Dad, Mom.

253
00:10:36,720 --> 00:10:37,670
Pour your parents a drink.

254
00:10:37,670 --> 00:10:38,120
Come, come.

255
00:10:38,120 --> 00:10:38,840
Here, Dad.

256
00:10:39,360 --> 00:10:40,630
Well, let's just have a sip.

257
00:10:40,630 --> 00:10:40,910
Dad.

258
00:10:41,120 --> 00:10:41,870
Here, Dad.

259
00:10:41,870 --> 00:10:42,270
Let me.

260
00:10:42,870 --> 00:10:44,270
Alright. This is enough.

261
00:10:44,630 --> 00:10:45,630
Come on, in-laws.

262
00:10:46,200 --> 00:10:46,750
So happy.

263
00:10:47,510 --> 00:10:48,630
Cheers.

264
00:10:50,440 --> 00:10:50,870
I...

265
00:10:52,270 --> 00:10:53,270
Where are you now?

266
00:10:53,550 --> 00:10:54,360
I'm in Nanlu,

267
00:10:54,550 --> 00:10:55,910
at the Municipal Procuratorate.

268
00:10:55,910 --> 00:10:57,170
At the procuratorate?

269
00:10:57,320 --> 00:10:58,120
That's great.

270
00:10:59,600 --> 00:11:00,960
I really have to thank you guys.

271
00:11:00,960 --> 00:11:01,960
If I hadn't met you,

272
00:11:01,960 --> 00:11:02,320
I really

273
00:11:02,320 --> 00:11:04,030
wouldn't have thought
of going for further studies.

274
00:11:04,030 --> 00:11:05,490
No, that's all down to you.

275
00:11:07,440 --> 00:11:08,720
Why didn't Zhang Lihui come?

276
00:11:08,720 --> 00:11:09,960
Where is she now?

277
00:11:10,720 --> 00:11:11,780
She's too far away.

278
00:11:11,840 --> 00:11:13,030
She was transferred to Bieshan.

279
00:11:13,030 --> 00:11:15,290
She's a prison resident prosecutor now.

280
00:11:15,480 --> 00:11:17,360
Why did she go there?

281
00:11:17,960 --> 00:11:19,080
Was it because

282
00:11:19,480 --> 00:11:20,510
with her husband?

283
00:11:20,870 --> 00:11:21,480
No.

284
00:11:21,510 --> 00:11:22,970
She's always been single.

285
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:26,800
She was just transferred there.

286
00:11:28,840 --> 00:11:29,440
Let's eat.

287
00:11:30,910 --> 00:11:31,790
Come, come.

288
00:11:32,200 --> 00:11:32,840
Court Pres. Ding.

289
00:11:32,840 --> 00:11:33,270
Yizhong.

290
00:11:33,270 --> 00:11:34,200
Congratulations.

291
00:11:34,200 --> 00:11:35,120
Thank you, everyone.

292
00:11:35,120 --> 00:11:35,720
Thank you.

293
00:11:35,910 --> 00:11:36,550
Have a seat.

294
00:11:36,550 --> 00:11:37,080
Sit, sit.

295
